{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794234545,"nonce":"tjuCUr/WUCm6eXAmQ7Db6//Lesc=","title":"A new tag name over a built-in face name leaves the new tag empty","message":"On a jno.shape.box domain, d.tag('xr', lambda x, y, z: x \u003e P - e) selects the same nodes as the built-in face 'right'. The node partition is exclusive, so 'xr' ends up with no nodes and a periodic tie on it fails with 'jno.fem periodic (N1E): boundary tag xr has no mesh vertices.' Re-tagging under the built-in name ('right') works. The error should say that the nodes are held by another tag, or the predicate should be evaluated inclusively as _face_nodes does when assembly boundary nodes are passed.","files":null}]}